From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FormalSnake <kyaniserni@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:55:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/27] gpui_linux: read a wayland or x11 window back in
 render_to_image

The Metal and DirectX renderers implement render_to_image; on Linux the default returned an
error, so a test could not capture a real window. The wgpu renderer draws the scene at the
drawable's size into an offscreen texture and reads it back as RGBA rows without presenting,
sharing the readback with the headless renderer. gpui exports RgbaImage under test-support,
which gpui_linux's test-support turns on, so neither crate's manifest changes.
